# .trivyignore — vulnerabilities suppressed for this repo's CI image scan.
#
# The CI security gate (gitleaks + trivy, fail-on-CRITICAL) reads this file
# automatically from the repo root. One vulnerability ID per line; blank lines
# and lines starting with '#' are ignored. Add an ID here ONLY after reviewing
# it — e.g. the CVE has no fix yet, or it isn't reachable in how we run the image.
#
# Prefer patching over suppressing: most OS CVEs are cleared by the
# `apt-get upgrade` / `apk upgrade` step already baked into the Dockerfile.
#
# The entry below is a placeholder to show the format — CVE-9999-9999 does not
# exist and matches nothing. Replace or delete it when you add real entries.
CVE-9999-9999
